; coverage test: the transitivity of `<` (number.kurt's `chain = <= <`, the generated rules
; "chain-trans-*") in a real proof -- Kurt's derivation is single-hop, so a < b < c < d needs an
; explicit intermediate a < c step. The four are constants: with `var a, b, c, d` (until 2026-10-14)
; `use c < d` was the schema `$c < $d`, "every number is less than every number", and `1 < 1`
; followed (found by the examples hunt).
load number
const a, b, c, d

use a < b
use b < c
use c < d

a < b and b < c
a < c
a < c and c < d
a < d
